@startuml
title Figure 2b — Hexagonal architecture — ports and adapters
left to right direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

actor "Customer Care\nOperator" as Operator

package "Driving adapters" {
  component "React operator UI" as UI
  component "Spring Security +\nHTTP adapter" as Http
}

interface "Inbound application use cases\ncustomer review · analysis · history" as Inbound
interface "CustomerActivityPort" as ActivityPort
interface "PolicyKnowledgePort" as PolicyPort
interface "AnalysisModelPort" as ModelPort
interface "AnalysisHistoryPort" as HistoryPort

hexagon "Application core\n\nidentity\ncustomer\nrisk\nanalysis\n\nproject-owned domain + application contracts" as Core

package "Driven adapters" {
  component "SyntheticActivityAdapter\nJpaCustomerActivityAdapter\n<<GoF Adapter>>" as ActivityAdapters
  component "StaticPolicyAdapter\nPgVectorPolicyAdapter\n<<GoF Adapter>>" as PolicyAdapters
  component "DeterministicAnalysisStub\nSpringAiAnalysisAdapter\n<<GoF Adapter>>" as ModelAdapters
  component "JpaAnalysisHistoryAdapter\n<<GoF Adapter>>" as HistoryAdapter
}

database "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as DB
component "External AI provider" as Provider <<external>>

Operator --> UI
UI --> Http : HTTP/JSON
Http --> Inbound
Inbound --> Core

Core --> ActivityPort
Core --> PolicyPort
Core --> ModelPort
Core --> HistoryPort

ActivityPort --> ActivityAdapters : interchangeable strategy implementations
PolicyPort --> PolicyAdapters : interchangeable strategy implementations
ModelPort --> ModelAdapters : interchangeable strategy implementations
HistoryPort --> HistoryAdapter

ActivityAdapters --> DB : JDBC when JPA selected
PolicyAdapters --> DB : JDBC/pgvector when R4 selected
HistoryAdapter --> DB : JDBC
ModelAdapters ..> Provider : HTTPS only when live adapter selected

note bottom of Core
  Hexagonal architecture is the architectural style, not a GoF pattern.
  GoF roles used inside it:
  - Adapter: infrastructure implementations translate external/framework APIs to ports.
  - Strategy: alternate implementations are selected behind stable port contracts.
  - Facade/application service: coarse-grained use cases orchestrate several ports
    without exposing that choreography to the HTTP adapter or UI.
end note
@enduml
